Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:08:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 60/61] [DSV4.1] Opt-in decode-shape FP8 GEMV for [32, 32]
 block scales on SM120 (recipe T3.41)

At decode M (<= 4) the tuned tensor-core tiles in w8a8_block_fp8_matmul_triton
(SWAP_AB / SPLIT_K, E20) stream the dense projection weights at ~780 GB/s on
the RTX PRO 6000 against a ~1,470 GB/s GDDR7 roof. fp8_gemv_dsv41 adds a plain
FP32-FMA row-dot: one CTA per BLOCK_N (<= 32, one block-scale row) output
columns, K in BLOCK_K contiguous slices, both scales folded into the activation,
M as a constexpr loop over the same weight slice, optional SPLIT_K through the
existing _reduce_block_fp8_split_k. Deterministic; not bit-identical to the
tensor-core path (FMA vs MMA accumulation order, <= 1 bf16 ulp observed).

Gated by SGLANG_DSV41_FP8_GEMV (default off) and used only for (N, K, M)
entries in configs/gemv,device_name=<dev>,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[32, 32].json.
The shipped RTX PRO 6000 table holds the 23/28 (shape, M) winners of a
423-config sweep (M=1: 4096x1280 6.7 -> 4.8 us, 16384x1280 26.9 -> 14.5 us,
25600x6144 201 -> 99 us); the five losers keep the Triton GEMM.

